**What happened**:
Virt-handler heartbeat causes the vm to be restarted when kubelet is restarted.

The virt-handler device_controller is watching the kubelet.sock file, and when kubelet restarts, `dpi.initialized` is set to `false`. **_If virt-handler executes a heartbeat  at this time_**, the `host-215.example/schedulable` label of the node will be set to `false`. After kubelet restarts, kubelet will kill pods that do not match the node label.（virt-launcher pod nodeSelector is `host-215.example/schedulable: "true"`）The virt-launcher pod will be killed by kubelet, causing the vm to restart.

related:
https://host-623.example/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/57355
https://host-623.example/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/70654
https://host-623.example/proj/proj/issues/71490

**How to reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)**:
Restart kubelet every 1s until the `host-215.example/schedulable` label on the node becomes `false`. Or delete virt-handler pod, set the `host-215.example/schedulable` label on the node to `false`, then restart kubelet.

**Environment**:
- Proj version (use `virtctl version`): 0.42.1
- Kubernetes version (use `kubectl version`): 1.22
